Clarifications: This is intended as a solution
for static documentation, not ephemeral notes.

| Knowledge Bases | Documentation/Wiki/Blogs | Books

Priorities(List):

  + Productivity: Tails aims to be the easiest way to
  professionally write documentation quickly for anything from a book to the total knowledge infrastructure of a F500 PaaS company.

  + Readability of PlainText: Less inline injection, plaintext is intended to be totally usable as is for a programmer.

  + Recursively Composable: -allow nested .tails rendering so many documents can be rendered as one larger .tails document, so documentation can be completely d.r.y-

  + Minimum tokenization latency: tokenization
  is inteded to be as minified as possible without losing plaintext readability.

  + optional DB based documentation: non monolithic documents are intended to be able to be requested, recieved and rendered as fast as possible. In a perfect world a tls bincode request could get the string, tokenize and switch it to the correct renderer function, which should theoretically maximize possible response time.

Inteded deps day 0;

